; Stage 1 of doc/rfc/draft-ndn-maru-typed-tree-matching-00.md: what we're building, how each piece relates to
; the others, and what would show it works.
;
; A Check is something the system can be asked.  notes/plan/observe.l asks every one with `observe`, whose answer is an
; Evidence value naming the code it ran against, and prints it as an event, `tree_lists do observed passed(tree: "1f3a...").`
; notes/plan/record appends those to evidence.john.  Replaying the events gives the chain of worlds, so `evidence` is the
; latest answer, and `at time` reads earlier ones.  An answer counts only for the code it ran against: plan-world.l makes
; `Now`, this tree, so a capability is proven only if its checks hold now.  Plans never run a check: rules read what's recorded.

start-world plan.
load "notes/plan/probes.l".

; what a check can answer: a law's verdict says more than yes or no
set Evidence = untested | passed(tree) | failed(tree)
  | tested(tree, trials) | proved(tree, cases) | refuted(tree, counterexample) | starved(tree, met, drawn)
  | vacuous(tree) | inconclusive(tree, input).
group Good passed tested proved.

group Check Case Measure Grammar Law.
create Case evidence.                                 ; a case in check/check.l
create Measure evidence command cadence.              ; a program; its exit status is the answer
create Grammar evidence file class rule host inherits samples.  ; compiled live, reading its own language
create Law evidence file support.                     ; one law, by name, of a law file

qualify Case observe is it case-passes.
qualify Measure observe is it command-succeeds.
qualify Grammar observe is it compiles-and-reads.
qualify Law observe is it law-verdict.

; which checks a plain `record` asks; `record full` asks them all
qualify Check routine if 1 = 1.
qualify Measure routine if its cadence = "routine".

; first, because what a whole run shows counts for the cases below, and they then needn't run again
make Measure WholeSuite untested "nice make check" "full".

make Case tree_selectors untested.
make Case tree_source untested.
make Case tree_lists untested.
make Case tree_args untested.
make Case tree_args_unread untested.
make Case tree_text_refuses untested.
make Case tree_interleave untested.
make Case tree_apply untested.
make Case tree_memo untested.
make Case tree_foreign untested.
make Case tree_literals untested.
make Case tree_parse_complete untested.
make Case tree_calc untested.

make Measure TextMatchingSpeed untested "notes/plan/speed" "routine".

make Grammar CExpressions untested "cexpr.g" "<cexpr>" "expression" "" [ ] [ "notes/plan/samples/cexpr.txt" ].
make Grammar JohnPrograms untested "john.g" "<john>" "program" "john.l" [ CExpressions ]
  [ "check/john/hanoi2.john", "check/john/x86-allocator.john", "check/john/airline.john" ].
make Grammar LawFiles untested "law.g" "<law>" "program" "law-compile.l" [ CExpressions ] [ "check/laws/cexpr.law" ].
make Grammar IrlPrograms untested "irl.g" "<irl>" "program" "compile-irl.l" [ CExpressions ] [ "test.irl", "dimacs.irl" ].
make Grammar Arm64Table untested "arm64.g" "<arm64spec>" "file" "" [ ] [ "arm64.spec" ].
make Grammar X86Table untested "x86.g" "<x86spec>" "file" "" [ ] [ "x86.spec" ].
make Grammar OsDefinitions untested "osdefs.g" "<osdefs>" "file" "compile-osdefs.l" [ ] [ "system.osdefs" ].
make Grammar TpegItself untested "tpeg.g" "<tpeg>" "parser_spec" "" [ ] [ "cexpr.g", "john.g" ].

make Law conditional_right untested "check/laws/cexpr.law" "".
make Law minus_left untested "check/laws/cexpr.law" "".
make Law comment_blank untested "check/laws/cexpr.law" "".

; an answer says which code gave it, and it's only good for that code
create Code tree.
action Check observed Answer consequence its evidence = Answer.
qualify Check holds if its evidence is Good and its evidence tree = Now tree.
qualify Check stale if its evidence is Good and not its evidence tree = Now tree.

; ---- what we're building
create Capability what where shown-by builds-on planned.

make Capability InputSelectors "a grammar reads its input only through in-head, in-tail and the other input selectors"
  "input.l" [ tree_selectors ] [ ] no.
make Capability AnySource "a grammar can match any source, each stream cell holding its head, lazy tail and memos"
  "source-parser.l" [ tree_source ] [ InputSelectors ] no.
make Capability ListPatterns "a rule can descend into a list and match inside it, as OMeta's form: does"
  "compile-tpeg.l, tpeg.g" [ tree_lists ] [ AnySource ] no.
make Capability ArgsOnInput "a rule's arguments are cells prepended to the stream on a source; on text they stay method arguments"
  "compile-tpeg.l" [ tree_args, tree_args_unread, tree_text_refuses ] [ ListPatterns ] no.
make Capability LiveGrammars "grammars compile in process, so code and grammar blocks can interleave on one input, and every grammar in the tree still compiles live and reads its language"
  "tpeg-repl.l, compile-tpeg.l" [ tree_interleave, conditional_right, minus_left, comment_blank, CExpressions, JohnPrograms, LawFiles, IrlPrograms, Arm64Table, X86Table, OsDefinitions, TpegItself ] [ AnySource ] no.
make Capability ApplyAndSuper "a rule named at run time can be applied, and an override can call its parent's rule"
  "compile-tpeg.l" [ tree_apply ] [ ArgsOnInput, LiveGrammars ] no.
make Capability MemosOnStream "the memo table lives on the stream, so a rule's answer is shared by whoever reads that cell"
  "source-parser.l" [ tree_memo ] [ ListPatterns ] no.
make Capability ForeignRules "a grammar can call another grammar's rule on the same input, with fresh memos, through a proxy cell"
  "source-parser.l, compile-tpeg.l" [ tree_foreign ] [ MemosOnStream ] no.
make Capability OneMatcherForAll "literals in a rule match what the source holds, and a file's grammar must parse completely"
  "compile-tpeg.l, tpeg.g" [ tree_literals, tree_parse_complete ] [ AnySource ] no.
make Capability EndToEnd "a calculator written as a grammar over trees runs with memos and arguments together"
  "check/tpeg-calc.l" [ tree_calc ] [ MemosOnStream, ArgsOnInput ] no.
make Capability TextStaysFast "text matching pays nothing for all this: within 15% of main's"
  "text-parser.l" [ TextMatchingSpeed ] [ AnySource ] no.
make Capability NothingElseBroke "every other check in the repository still passes"
  "the whole tree" [ WholeSuite ] [ EndToEnd, ForeignRules ] no.

; ---- how the pieces relate
; nothing shown is nothing proven
qualify Capability proven if its shown-by size > 0 and for every its shown-by do each holds = yes.
qualify Capability done if it proven = yes or it planned = yes.
qualify Capability ready if for every its builds-on do each done = yes.
rel-qualify Capability:A depends-on Capability:B if B in A builds-on.
rel-qualify Check:C supports Capability:K if C in K shown-by.

; ---- what the history says, for reading, never for planning
qualify Check regressed if not its evidence is Good and not its evidence is untested
  and for some time A up to time do (at time A its evidence is Good).
qualify Check observed-within: N if
  for some time A after (time - N) up to time do (at time A it did observed).

; ---- the goal
create Team.
make Team T.
action Team build Capability consequence Capability planned = yes.
rule Team build is Capability done = no.
rule Team build is Capability ready = yes.
goal Team deliver try for every all Capability do each done = yes.
; every capability, in some order that respects builds-on: no choice to search among
goal-strategy Team deliver sat.
